Time Limit: 1 sec
Memory: 256 MB

Description
You are given two strings of equal length, originalUrl and targetUrl, each consisting of lowercase English letters. You are also given an integer cost — the maximum total amount you are allowed to spend to transform a contiguous substring of originalUrl into the corresponding substring of targetUrl.

Changing a character at index i costs the absolute difference of their ASCII values:

diff(i) = |ASCII(originalUrl[i]) − ASCII(targetUrl[i])|

Find the maximum length of a substring of originalUrl that can be transformed into the corresponding substring of targetUrl with total cost ≤ cost. If no such substring exists, output 0.

Input Format
The input consists of T test cases. For each test case:
An integer n — the length of the strings.
A string originalUrl of length n.
A string targetUrl of length n.
An integer cost — the maximum allowed total cost.

Output Format
For each test case, output a single integer — the maximum length of a transformable substring with total cost ≤ cost.

Constraints
1 ≤ t ≤ 10
1 ≤ n ≤ 10⁷
originalUrl, targetUrl ∈ a, …, zⁿ
0 ≤ cost ≤ 10⁹

Sample Input 1

```text
1
6
adpgki
cdmxki
6
```

Sample Output 1

```text
3
```

Sample Input 2

```text
1
4
abcd
bcdf
3
```

Sample Output 2

```text
3
```

Note

First sample:
Per-index costs are [|a − c| = 2, |d − d| = 0, |p − m| = 3, |g − x| = 17, |k − k| = 0, |i − i| = 0] = [2, 0, 3, 17, 0, 0].

The longest contiguous segment with total cost ≤ 6 is indices 0..2 (substring "adp") with total cost 2 + 0 + 3 = 5, so the answer is 3.



#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
typedef long long ll;
#define endl "\n"   // optional, better to avoid redefining endl

void solve() {
    int n;
    cin>>n;
    string org,tar;
    cin>>org>>tar;
    int cost = 0;
    cin>>cost;

    vector<int>diff(n);

    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if(org[i] != tar[i])
        {
            diff[i] = abs((org[i] - 'a') - (tar[i] - 'a'));
        }
        else
        {
            diff[i] = 0;
        }
    }

    int ans = 0;

    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        int sum = 0;
        for(int j = i;j <n; j++)
        {
            sum += diff[j];
            if(sum <= cost)
            {
                ans = max(ans, j - i + 1);
            }
        }
    }
    cout<<" "<<endl;
    cout<<ans<<endl;
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t;
    cin >> t;
    while (t--) {
        solve();
    }

    return 0;
}


